Spec: Actual protected Linux server verification

Purpose:
  Exercise persistent server lifecycle on an explicitly selected local Linux host without cloud deployment.

Owns:
  ./verify.ps1
  ./README.md

References:
  /control-plane/serverhost/serverhost.sdd
  /backend-frp/overlays/cmd/linkgate-server/main.sdd

Must:
  Use only a new ignored artifact directory and a specified WSL distribution; temporary state is created and removed by owned test lifetimes inside Linux.
  Build from a verified derived pinned backend with the new server command and use native Linux execution for permission/locking checks rather than treating Windows skips as passing host evidence.
  Bound test execution, preserve aggregate logs and binary hashes, and keep installed services, global networking, physical phones and ECS unchanged.
  Distinguish local host validation from production deployment, public network traversal and full release readiness.
